---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="How we review"
	description="How Level 2 Home EV Chargers sources specs, writes verdicts, and handles affiliate links."
	canonicalPath="about/"
>
	<article class="article">
		<h1 class="page-title">How we review</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			This is a small, sourced directory of home Level 2 EV charging stations (EVSE). It is
			not a lab test program and not a shopping ranking with invented scores.
		</p>

		<h2>What a page has to include</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Who the unit is for, in plain language.</li>
			<li>Key specs — amperage, connector, cable length, install options, smart features — only when a cited source states them.</li>
			<li>An honest verdict drawn from those sources, including drawbacks.</li>
			<li>A sources list with real URLs.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Where facts come from</h2>
		<p>
			Every charger page should cite the manufacturer (product page, datasheet, or install guide)
			plus at least two independent reviews when they exist. Preferred independent outlets include
			Wirecutter, CNET, and Car and Driver. If a review is paywalled or blocked, we do not
			paraphrase it from a third-party summary.
		</p>
		<p>
			Manufacturer range-per-hour figures are estimates. They depend on the vehicle, weather,
			and the circuit the unit is set to. We label them as manufacturer estimates.
		</p>

		<h2>What we will not invent</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Specs, prices, star ratings, or traffic numbers.</li>
			<li>A current street price when listings disagree or a review widget shows a live marketplace figure. In those cases <code>approxPriceUsd</code> stays empty.</li>
			<li>Affiliate checkout links. Until a program is approved, buy links go only to the manufacturer and are labeled as non-affiliate.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Corrections</h2>
		<p>
			If a manufacturer updates a datasheet or a cited review changes, the page should be revised
			and the <code>lastUpdated</code> date changed. Old prices from reviews stay attributed to
			that review; they are not treated as today’s price.
		</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
